/// <summary>
/// Server only. A table for a board or card game: a board of rows and columns at a place in the
/// world, pieces that stand on its cells and move between them, seats with a turn order, bets and
/// save/load. You write the game's rules; the table does the rest. Every player of the table's
/// dimension sees the pieces (they are props), and a player who joins later sees the board as it
/// is. Near a free seat a player gets a 'Sit down' hint (U); seated, they point at a cell with the
/// crosshair, or, with a camera shot of the table's or their seat's own, with the mouse pointer
/// over the board as the game's dice players do, and click with mouse 1 or Enter; the arrow keys
